{"id":"mahabharata-7-136","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":136,"title":"षट्त्रिंशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 136 · Night: the Pandavas press Ashvatthaman","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira and Bhima, with Arjuna on the right, attack Ashvatthaman and the Kaurava division. Corpses and severed elephant trunks lie everywhere and many kings abandon their vehicles and flee.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ, ಭೀಮರು ಬಲಭಾಗದಲ್ಲಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನೊಡನೆ ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಮತ್ತು ಕೌರವ ದಳದ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಎಲ್ಲೆಡೆ ಶವ, ಕತ್ತರಿಸಿದ ಆನೆ ಸೊಂಡಿಲುಗಳು ಬಿದ್ದಿವೆ; ಅನೇಕ ರಾಜರು ವಾಹನ ಬಿಟ್ಟು ಓಡುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर और भीम, दाईं ओर अर्जुन के साथ, अश्वत्थामा और कौरव दल पर आक्रमण करते हैं। सब ओर शव और कटी गज-सूँड़ें पड़ी हैं, और अनेक राजा वाहन छोड़कर भाग जाते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు, భీముడు కుడివైపు అర్జునునితో కలిసి అశ్వత్థామపై, కౌరవ దళంపై దాడి చేస్తారు. అంతటా శవాలు, తెగిన ఏనుగు తొండాలు పడి ఉంటాయి; అనేక రాజులు వాహనాలు వదిలి పారిపోతారు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரரும் பீமனும் வலப்பக்கம் அர்ஜுனனுடன் அஸ்வத்தாமனையும் கௌரவ அணியையும் தாக்குகின்றனர். எங்கும் உடல்களும் வெட்டுண்ட யானைத் துதிக்கைகளும் கிடக்க, பல மன்னர் வாகனங்களை விட்டு ஓடுகின்றனர்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരനും ഭീമനും, വലതുഭാഗത്ത് അർജുനനും, അശ്വത്ഥാമാവിനെയും കൗരവ വിഭാഗത്തെയും ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു. ശവങ്ങളും മുറിഞ്ഞ ആനത്തുമ്പികളും എല്ലായിടത്തും കിടക്കുന്നു; പല രാജാക്കന്മാരും തങ്ങളുടെ വാഹനങ്ങൾ ഉപേക്ഷിച്ച് ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.136; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरश्चैव भीमसेनश्च पाण्डवः ।\nद्रोणपुत्रं महाराज समन्तात्पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira and the Pandava Bhimasena surrounded Drona's son on all sides, great king."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा भारद्वाजेन संवृतः ।\nअभ्ययात्पाण्डवान्संख्ये ततो युद्धमवर्तत ।\nघोररूपं महाराज भीरूणां भयवर्धनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana, accompanied by Drona (Bharadvaja's son), advanced against the Pandavas in battle, and a terrible fight followed, O great king, that raised fear in cowards."}},{"n":3,"text":"अम्बष्ठान्मालवान्वङ्गाञ्शिबींस्त्रैगर्तकानपि ।\nप्राहिणोन्मृत्युलोकाय गणान्क्रुद्धो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In anger, Yudhishthira sent the Ambashthas, Malavas, Vangas, Shibis and Trigartas to the world of death in whole bands."}},{"n":4,"text":"अभीषाहाञ्शूरसेनान्क्षत्रियान्युद्धदुर्मदान् ।\nनिकृत्य पृथिवीं चक्रे भीमः शोणितकर्दमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima cut down the Abhishahas, the Shurasenas and the kshatriyas fierce in battle, and made the earth a mire of blood."}},{"n":5,"text":"यौधेयारट्टराजन्यान्मद्रकांश्च गणान्युधि ।\nप्राहिणोन्मृत्युलोकाय किरीटी निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kiritin (Arjuna) with sharp arrows sent the Yaudheyas, the Arattas' princes and the Madrakas to the world of death in battle."}},{"n":6,"text":"प्रगाढमञ्जोगतिभिर्नाराचैरभिपीडिताः ।\nनिपेतुर्द्विरदा भूमौ द्विशृङ्गा इव पर्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by iron arrows that went deep and straight, elephants fell to the ground like two-peaked mountains."}},{"n":7,"text":"निकृत्तैर्हस्तिहस्तैश्च लुठमानैस्ततस्ततः ।\nरराज वसुधा कीर्णा विसर्पद्भिरिवोरगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth, strewn with severed trunks of elephants rolling here and there, looked as if covered by crawling snakes."}},{"n":8,"text":"क्षिप्तैः कनकचित्रैश्च नृपच्छत्रैः क्षितिर्बभौ ।\nद्यौरिवादित्यचन्द्राद्यैर्ग्रहैः कीर्णा युगक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"The ground, scattered with the royal umbrellas flung down, bright with gold, shone like the sky at the world's end strewn with the sun, moon and other planets."}},{"n":9,"text":"हत प्रहरताभीता विध्यत व्यवकृन्तत ।\nइत्यासीत्तुमुलः शब्दः शोणाश्वस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Kill! Strike! Do not be afraid! Pierce! Cut them down!\" So a tumultuous shout arose around the chariot of the red-horsed Drona."}},{"n":10,"text":"द्रोणस्तु परमक्रुद्धो वायव्यास्त्रेण संयुगे ।\nव्यधमत्तान्यथा वायुर्मेघानिव दुरत्ययः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Drona, in a great rage, scattered them in battle with the Vayavya weapon, as wind drives off clouds, irresistible."}},{"n":11,"text":"ते हन्यमाना द्रोणेन पाञ्चालाः प्राद्रवन्भयात् ।\nपश्यतो भीमसेनस्य पार्थस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck down by Drona, the Panchalas fled in fear, while Bhimasena and the great-souled Partha looked on."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततः किरीटी भीमश्च सहसा संन्यवर्तताम् ।\nमहता रथवंशेन परिगृह्य बलं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kiritin and Bhima suddenly turned back, surrounding your force with a great mass of chariots."}},{"n":13,"text":"बीभत्सुर्दक्षिणं पार्श्वमुत्तरं तु वृकोदरः ।\nभारद्वाजं शरौघाभ्यां महद्भ्यामभ्यवर्षताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bibhatsu on the right flank and Vrikodara on the left rained two great floods of arrows on Bharadvaja's son."}},{"n":14,"text":"तौ तदा सृञ्जयाश्चैव पाञ्चालाश्च महारथाः ।\nअन्वगच्छन्महाराज मत्स्याश्च सह सोमकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Srinjayas and the great-warrior Panchalas, and the Matsyas with the Somakas, followed those two, great king."}},{"n":15,"text":"तथैव तव पुत्रस्य रथोदाराः प्रहारिणः ।\nमहत्या सेनया सार्धं जग्मुर्द्रोणरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And likewise your son's noble chariot-fighters, striking hard, went with a great army toward Drona's chariot."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततः सा भारती सेना वध्यमाना किरीटिना ।\nतमसा निद्रया चैव पुनरेव व्यदीर्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that Bharata army, struck by Kiritin, was again shattered, by darkness and by sleep."}},{"n":17,"text":"द्रोणेन वार्यमाणास्ते स्वयं तव सुतेन च ।\nन शक्यन्ते महाराज योधा वारयितुं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Although held back by Drona and by your son himself, the warriors could not be restrained then, O great king."}},{"n":18,"text":"सा पाण्डुपुत्रस्य शरैर्दार्यमाणा महाचमूः ।\nतमसा संवृते लोके व्यद्रवत्सर्वतोमुखी ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great force, torn by the arrows of Pandu's son, fled in all directions in the darkness that covered the world."}},{"n":19,"text":"उत्सृज्य शतशो वाहांस्तत्र केचिन्नराधिपाः ।\nप्राद्रवन्त महाराज भयाविष्टाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some kings, great king, gave up hundreds of their mounts and fled on every side, seized by fear."}}]}]}